                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Layup feels like it's bringing an additional layer of depth brought to the 2d arena fighter formula. The goal of scoring on the enemy team instead of just getting the most kills in a match makes this game feel familiar to people that have played games like Smash but distinct enough to stand on its own two feet. It's easy to pick up but, thanks to the variety of abilities and techniques you can employ, it has a surprising depth that'll leave you saying \"how did you do that?\". Layup is a fun game to play solo or with friends. Load up a 2v2 lobby and you'll see the hours fly by.",
